Adding to Ed's comments. Withe standardized items you can use N(0, 1) for most repressions/factor loadings/intercepts priors.

About the model comment, I agree with Ed, I think you have misspeciefd the latent change score.

You can check this syntax for a an example of a "simple" shcnage score model

change21_mod <- '
### latent true scores
PT1 =~ 1*NegT1
PT2 =~ 1*NegT2

PT1 ~~ NA*PT1
PT2 ~~ 0*PT2

PT1 ~1
PT2 ~0*1

NegT1 ~0*1
NegT2 ~0*1

NegT1 ~~ uv*NegT1
NegT2 ~~ uv*NegT2

### autoregressions
PT2 ~ 1*PT1

### latent change scores
change_21 =~ 1*PT2

change_21 ~c(m1)*1
change_21 ~~ c(v1)*change_21
'

